# JES keyboard actions
@scenario tutorial_lesson_49
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/scenes/input_lab.jes]
[set tutorial_excerpt bindings]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Each line binds a key press to a named action. The block passes arguments to that action. C places a circle on the left. B places a box on the right.
@label lab
> Run the keyboard lab -> demo
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label demo
[jes push scripts/scenes/input_lab.jes label compare]
@label compare
ginger: Try changing r from 28 to 42, then rerun the lab. The circle should grow at the same spawn point.
[jump lab]
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_49]
[flag tutorial_done_49]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_9]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Keep C as the spawn key and move its circle farther right. Which parameter should you edit?
> Increase x. -> practice_result
> Increase r. -> practice_hint
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: The action reads x and y as coordinates. It reads r as the radius.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: Increase x and keep r fixed. Rerun the lab to compare the two spawn positions.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Which part assigns the B key its behavior?
> The action name after do. -> correct
> The height inside the argument block. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
ginger: The key picks which binding to run. The action name picks the behavior.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: Exactly. spawnBox creates the box and reads w and h as its dimensions.
> Replay example -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
